    mutate::list::tests::a_break_given_on_the_command_line_is_one_of_its_own
    mutate::drive::tests::a_break_given_on_its_own_is_run_once_and_its_result_is_never_a_lists

[break] one-off-has-one-name-for-all-text
rule: A break given with `--break` is named for what it is made of, so that the same text is the same break and another text is another.
file: xtask/src/mutate/list.rs
in: to_break
find: hash.0 >> 32
replace: 0
caught-by:
    mutate::list::tests::a_break_given_on_the_command_line_is_one_of_its_own

[break] one-off-takes-a-file-outside-the-repository
rule: The file of a break given with `--break` is a path inside the repository, as in a list.
file: xtask/src/mutate/list.rs
in: to_break
find: if !is_repository_path(&file) {
replace: if false {
caught-by:
    mutate::list::tests::a_break_given_on_the_command_line_is_refused_for_what_a_list_would_refuse

[break] one-off-takes-occurrence-zero
rule: An occurrence is counted from 1, here as in a list.
file: xtask/src/mutate/list.rs
in: to_break
find: if self.occurrence == Some(0) {
replace: if false {
caught-by:
    mutate::list::tests::a_break_given_on_the_command_line_is_refused_for_what_a_list_would_refuse

[break] one-off-goes-with-a-lists-names
rule: A break given with `--break` is refused beside break names, a list's name and `--file`.
file: xtask/src/mutate/mod.rs
in: refuse_what_does_not_go_together
find: if !self.only.is_empty() || !self.files.is_empty() {
